# IMPLEMENTATION RULES

Follow these rules throughout the implementation.

### Rule 1 — Inspect before modifying
Identify the relevant files, functions, database tables, triggers, and configuration before changing anything.

### Rule 2 — Preserve the current architecture
Use the existing React/TypeScript and Supabase implementation. Do not rebuild the application or introduce a separate authentication system.

### Rule 3 — Fix the root causes
Correct the redirect configuration, callback handling, and role-assignment logic. Do not hide errors or implement a frontend-only workaround.

### Rule 4 — Protect privileged roles
Never trust an unvalidated client-supplied role as authorization. Preserve backend validation, RLS, and existing approval requirements.

### Rule 5 — Preserve existing data
Do not delete, recreate, or indiscriminately update user accounts, profiles, or role associations.

### Rule 6 — Avoid unrelated changes
Do not redesign unrelated pages, change the application's branding, or modify unrelated AgriCycle features.

### Rule 7 — Keep configuration secure
Do not place Supabase service-role keys, private credentials, or other secrets in client-side code.

### Rule 8 — Do not invent deployment details
Use the verified production URL and existing routing setup. If the necessary configuration is unavailable, clearly identify what needs to be configured.

### Rule 9 — Handle database changes carefully
If schema modifications are necessary, inspect dependencies and existing records first. Use a migration that preserves data and does not weaken constraints or RLS.

### Rule 10 — Report actual results
Do not claim that the confirmation email, deployment, Supabase dashboard, or production environment has been fixed unless the relevant configuration was actually changed and verified.

